 "howCounted": "Valued two-sided trades in the selected seasons and league-year stretches. Prices are anchored to a next-draft first-round pick. At least 80 trades for the whole view, 60 per half or window, and 8 delivery records with at least 0.5 forecast wins. Delivered wins are compared with the forecast at trade time. Ranges carry price and delivery uncertainty. The going rate is the asset-count-weighted median across positions and picks, never a live quote. Asset comparisons need 25 legs of the other kind. Stretch prices need 60 trades, 12 legs of this kind, and a bounded price error; only a stretch beating every other known stretch beyond chance is marked. Returns are the opposite side's forecast wins, not realised delivery. Buyers are franchise standing at trade time, not today's owner identity."
